"Tianlan (Tianlan Shan) is the living Earth Spirit, the dragon, of the Azure Hills."
"The sects do not know Tianlan's true nature or the truth of the old provincial formation."
"Tianlan appears as a small young girl of stone with ancient eyes."
"Tianlan and the spirit Jiguang are siblings, both made by the Great Ancestor Shennong."
"Tianlan is bound in pact to Jin and Meiling, her Connected Ones, by golden threads."
"Tianlan feels her Connected Ones' pain and injuries as her own, and they feel hers."
"Jin speaks with Tianlan in his mind; she can also speak to him from her Spirit Realm."
"Those who dream while resting at Fa Ram can sometimes glimpse Tianlan's realm."
"Tianlan lives in a cottage deep underground, tied to Jin's Qi."
"A snowman spirit, the General That Commands the Winter, guards Tianlan's cottage."
"The General That Commands the Winter swore fealty to Tianlan's throne as a minor land spirit."
"Tianlan sleeps through much of winter, still giving Fa Ram a faint protective pulse of Qi."
"Signs of Tianlan at Hong Yaowu: a golden-cracked girl, peach scent, an old man's laugh."
"Tianlan bears golden seams like mended pottery from the Breaking; she leaks ichor if overtaxed."
"Tianlan was badly wounded again in last winter's solstice demon attack."
"Only Jin's direct presence lets Tianlan fully repair her worst wounds."
"Joint breathing and martial training with her Connected One slowly mend Tianlan's veins."
"Tianlan's Dragon Veins carry her Qi like blood; damage to them causes her real pain."
"Tianlan's veins run broken through the Grand Ravine, garbling her partner's Qi sense there."
"Tianlan's veins under the Grass Sea can rupture, bleeding Qi into the air."
"Tianlan can feel formations driven into the earth."
"Tianlan can send small tendrils of herself to watch over distant people."
"Tianlan can reach any place her Connected Ones have blessed or repaired."
"Tianlan can't easily sense Qi taken up by plants; they absorb it too slowly."
"Tianlan can steady the Earth Spirit beneath the Misty Lake in person."
"Tianlan cannot directly harm Spirit Beasts of the physical world, only curse them."
"Tianlan hides her pain out of habit; Jin gently discourages this self-sacrifice."
"Tianlan holds a void power that devours foes and feeds on their Qi; she fears to use it."
"Born of despair, Tianlan's void power would consume the world to save those she loves."
"Tianlan is fragmented and slowly regaining her memories."
"Tianlan relives Shennong's ancient teachings as core memories within her."
"The forest guardian Mishu once mentored Tianlan."
"Xiaoshi was Tianlan's Connected One before Jin; she remembers him fondly."
"Xiaoshi never grew his Earth Spirit's strength, only his access to it."
"Tianlan and Xiaoshi swore brotherhood with the Grand Ravine."
"Shenguashi is a memory-crystal spirit of Xiaoshi's, set to guard Tianlan and find an Emperor."
"Shenguashi is trapped in a crystal but can ride copied memory streams beyond it."
"The ancient formation that once empowered, then destroyed, Tianlan can safely heal land."
"Tianlan's tracking thread into the Ash Forest shattered in the solstice battle."
"Tianlan's spilled blood pooled into a golden spring at the ruined heart of the Ash Forest."
"Monstrous mutations near the Ash Forest come from creatures drinking Tianlan's blood."
"This spring Tianlan is still healing her solstice wounds while Jin travels south."
